---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="MYST: The Book — Dmitrii Zhukov">
  <section class="px-6 pt-16 pb-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-4">CH 03</p>
      <h1 class="font-display text-6xl font-semibold uppercase tracking-tight md:text-7xl">MYST: The Book</h1>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-4xl text-lg text-ink-dim">
        <i>Myst</i> is a supernatural mystery novel about unexplained disappearances in the isolated Alaskan town of Mag Point. Wrapped in dense coastal fog, the town hides horrors that its residents refuse to speak of, and the truth behind them is far darker than anyone can imagine. 
        <b> STATIC</b> is a narrative-driven psychological horror game based on the novel, retelling and expanding its story through exploration, investigation, and survival.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-12 grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-[260px_1fr]">

        <!-- cover + editions -->
        <div>
          <img src="/myst/myst-1.png" alt="Myst cover"
               class="aspect-[4/5.7] w-full border border-line object-cover" />

          <div class="book-links">
            <p class="book-links__label">// Editions</p>
            <a class="book-links__item" href="#" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
              <span class="book-links__store">Litres</span>
              <span class="book-links__meta">Russian · 2025</span>
            </a>
            <a class="book-links__item" href="#" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
              <span class="book-links__store">Amazon Kindle</span>
              <span class="book-links__meta">English · 2026</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- annotation -->
        <div class="space-y-5 text-ink-dim">
          <dl class="book-meta">
            <div>
              <dt>Genre</dt>
              <dd>Mystery horror</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Length</dt>
              <dd>457 pages</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Setting</dt>
              <dd>Mag Point, Alaska · 2008 / 2018</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>

          <p>
            August 2018. Saoirse Barrell reluctantly returns to Mag Point, a remote port town 
            on Baranof Island, Alaska. She has not set foot in the state in ten years, not 
            since the summer her younger brother Caleb vanished along with four other children. 
            The town remembers that summer for one other thing as well: the return of a 
            strange television broadcast that should never have been seen again.
          </p>
          <p>
            Now people are disappearing again. To uncover the truth, Saoirse must stand 
            beside Ian Demme, her high school sweetheart, whom she left behind in 2008 
            without a word of goodbye.
          </p>
          <p>
            Ian has his own theory about the signal and the thing that hides behind it. 
            Together, they begin an investigation of their own, one that will drag them 
            deeper into Mag Point's long-buried secrets.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

        <figure class="book-quote">
            <blockquote>
              <p>Then everything changed, when a thick, clinging mist came barreling in off 
                the sea and swallowed the handful of clear days the northern summer 
                had to offer.</p>
            </blockquote>
            <figcaption>Myst, Episode [02]</figcaption>
        </figure>


      <!-- excerpts -->
      <section id="excerpts" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 border-t border-line pt-10">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl uppercase tracking-tight text-ink">Excerpts</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-ink-dim">Three scenes from the English edition.</p>

      <div class="mt-8 space-y-6">

        <article class="excerpt">
          <p class="excerpt__title">Saoirse is alone in the hotel room</p>
          <img class="excerpt__img" src="/myst/excerpt-1.png" alt="" loading="lazy" />
          <div class="excerpt__body">
            <p>While Saoirse was pondering how best to tell her young man that she would be forced to linger in town a while longer, the words being spoken from the news studio began to reach her awareness:</p>
            <p><i>"And now to regional news. In the town of Mag Point, Alaska, a local resident was detained this morning on suspicion of the kidnapping and murder of Kyren Hall, nine years old. The suspect in the crime is Val Barrell, ship's mechanic of the fishing trawler Santiago and father of Saoirse and Caleb Barrell."</i></p>
            <p>Saoirse did not notice herself rising to her feet, unable to believe what she was hearing.</p>
            <p>The anchor droned on, imperturbable:</p>
            <p><i>"Saoirse Barrell is known for having left Mag Point in August of two thousand eight while her younger brother, Caleb, still remained in the status of..."</i></p>
            <p>Saoirse tore the power cable from the socket in one sharp motion and, breathing fast and shallow, stared at the matte surface of the television screen. From the sudden fright the girl's heart was hammering somewhere at her throat, and her legs had gone to cotton.</p>
            <p>"Missing," the sentence was finished directly above Saoirse's left ear.</p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="excerpt">
          <p class="excerpt__title">Saoirse drives half-conscious Ian to Donal's for help</p>
          <img class="excerpt__img" src="/myst/excerpt-2.png" alt="" loading="lazy" />
          <div class="excerpt__body">
            <p>The beige Ford Ranger raced down the empty road; Saoirse yanked the balky gearshift, and the transmission creaked as though the truck was about to come apart at the seams. Ian sat in the passenger seat, wrapped in a gray blanket. He seemed to be unconscious, but when the vehicle jolted over another bump, Demme turned to the girl and asked:</p>
            <p>"Did you take the laptop?"</p>
            <p>"It's on the back seat."</p>
            <p>"Good. If I black out again, there's a red syringe in the glove box. The injection has to go into a vein."</p>
            <p>Saoirse said nothing, but nodded to show she had understood it all.</p>
            <p>"You're bleeding," Demme said after a pause.</p>
            <p>"I'm okay. You sure he'll be there?"</p>
            <p>"He moonlights at the Fisherman's Daughter after hours. Sleeps in the back room," Ian answered.</p>
            <p>"Good Lord..." was all Saoirse could bring out. "What happened to him?"</p>
            <p>"I don't know. We hardly ever speak."</p>
            <p>"Never would have thought that Donal..."</p>
            <p>"Would you have thought that I?" Ian smiled weakly.</p>
            <p>"I didn't think about you at all, Ian," Saoirse answered sharply. 
              "And let's not talk about this anymore. I am sorry for what I said to 
              you yesterday, I didn't mean any of it. But that is all I am going to 
              say to you."</p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="excerpt">
          <p class="excerpt__title">Donal Hockley tries to get information from the widow of August Pruett</p>
          <img class="excerpt__img" src="/myst/excerpt-3.png" alt="" loading="lazy" />
          <div class="excerpt__body">
            <p>"Good afternoon, Ma'am," Hockley said with a courteous smile when a short elderly woman in horn-rimmed glasses appeared behind the dusty screen of the outer shutter. She was somewhat stout and slightly pigeon-toed, but moved quite nimbly for her age.</p>
            <p>"My name is Donal Hockley, I'm a chief petty officer of the United States Coast Guard. Can I speak with August Pruett, please?"</p>
            <p>Donal had absolutely no plan in his head, so he had decided that the best strategy for making the widow's acquaintance would be to pretend he did not know of Pruett's death.</p>
            <p>"Only if you have a Ouija board with you," came the answer. "August Pruett passed away eight years ago."</p>
            <p>"I'm very sorry to hear it," Donal said in a mournful voice.</p>
            <p>"How did you know my husband?" the woman asked with slight suspicion, opening the outer door. "You're far too young to have known him from the service."</p>
            <p>A formidable old lady, the young man thought to himself, and answered:</p>
            <p>"I have been working in an archive, reading through the materials, and I came across documents signed by Corporal Pruett. They're old reports on the decryption of intercepted signals. Some parts struck me as strange."</p>
            <p>"You're speaking of the Gray Signal, are you not?" the widow interrupted him, and sighed: "Of course you are. Well, I'm not surprised. I always knew that someday someone would come for answers. Though in my imagination it was the military police."</p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>

      </section>

      <!-- funnel to the game -->
      <aside class="book-next">
        <p class="book-next__label">// From page to play</p>
        <p class="book-next__body">
          The novel gave <b>STATIC</b> its town, its characters and its ending. The game takes all three away
          from the reader and hands them to the player. Now it's your choice, and it doesn't 
          have to go the way the book went.
        </p>
        <a class="book-next__cta" href="/game">See the game &#8594;</a>
      </aside>

    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>